* =====================================================================
*  Local ngspice equivalents of the Circuit Studio active devices.
*
*  Circuit Studio implements OTA / OPAMP natively.  ngspice does not
*  (its 'O' card is a lossy line and XSPICE ships no opamp/ota model),
*  so these are behavioural equivalents built from the parameters the
*  netlists themselves declare:
*
*    O  p n cv out  <OTA model>   IS VT VPOS VNEG VDROPPOS VDROPNEG
*         Iout = Iabc * tanh(Vd / (2*VT))      Iabc = V(cv)  [amps]
*         (positive: sources current into `out` when V(p) > V(n);
*          sim.py swaps the inputs for the opposite polarity)
*
*    A  inp inn out <OPAMP model> aol gbp rin rout vsat
*         one pole at gbp/aol, hard limit at +/- vsat, output rout.
*
*  Validated against the published database netlists: see NOTES.md
* =====================================================================

.subckt OTA p n cv out
Bgm  0 out I = V(cv) * tanh((V(p)-V(n))/0.0517)
Rlk  out 0 1G
.ends OTA

.subckt OPA inp inn out params: aol=2e5 gbp=3e6 rout=75 vsat=13 pole=3e1
Rin  inp inn 1e12
Gd   0 n1 inp inn 1
Rd   n1 0 {aol}
Cd   n1 0 {1/(2*3.14159265358979*aol*pole)}
Bl   o0 0 V = max(-{vsat}, min({vsat}, V(n1)))
Rout o0 out {rout}
Rlk  out 0 1G
.ends OPA
